Fortunately, drivers tend to act within a reasonable and consistent range, and therefore the flow of traffic tends to have a certain degree of reasonable consistency, which can mathematically roughly represent.
In order to better represent the flow of traffic, a relationship has been established between the three main characteristics: (1) flow, (2) density, and (3) velocity.
These relationships are useful for the planning, design and operation of road facilities.
